From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:46:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: restore station flags on association

The DISASSOC event clears wcid.sta and sets wcid.sta_disabled, but the
ASSOC event restores neither. A station that moves from ASSOC to AUTH
and back on the same link keeps sta cleared, so wcid_to_sta() returns
NULL and RX statistics, power save transitions and TX status for it
are lost until it is removed. mt7915 already sets both flags on ASSOC;
do the same for mt7996.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/main.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -1497,6 +1497,8 @@ mt7996_mac_sta_links_event(struct mt7996
 				return err;
 
 			msta_link->wcid.tx_info |= MT_WCID_TX_INFO_SET;
+			msta_link->wcid.sta = 1;
+			msta_link->wcid.sta_disabled = 0;
 			break;
 		case MT76_STA_EVENT_AUTHORIZE:
 			err = mt7996_mcu_add_sta(dev, link_conf, link_sta,
